From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Subject: [PATCH] media: iris: register the encoder on SM8350 again

0021 stopped registering /dev/video1 on qcom,sm8350-iris because using
the encoder crashed the VPU firmware. No log of that crash was kept.
A bare open() does not reach the firmware for the encoder: the HFI
session is opened at REQBUFS (iris_vb2_queue_setup), and the
uninitialised uncompressed input packet that 0021 now zeroes is only
sent once input buffers are queued. If the crash happened at session
init, the memset does not fix it. Register the encoder like on every
other platform so this can be tested.

Kept separate from the decode-order patches so the encoder can be
dropped again on its own if the firmware still crashes.

Signed-off-by: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_probe.c |   14 +++-----------
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_probe.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_probe.c
index b417a5f..b628747 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_probe.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_probe.c
@@ -278,17 +278,9 @@ static int iris_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	if (ret)
 		goto err_v4l2_unreg;
 
-	/*
-	 * The SM8350 VPU firmware (vpu20_4v on the Galaxy Z Flip3) crashes
-	 * when the encoder node is opened, and the cause is not known yet.
-	 * Keep the encoder off there only: SM8250 runs the same HFI Gen1
-	 * encoder path upstream, and the other platforms are unaffected.
-	 */
-	if (!of_device_is_compatible(dev->of_node, "qcom,sm8350-iris")) {
-		ret = iris_register_video_device(core, ENCODER);
-		if (ret)
-			goto err_vdev_unreg_dec;
-	}
+	ret = iris_register_video_device(core, ENCODER);
+	if (ret)
+		goto err_vdev_unreg_dec;
 
 	platform_set_drvdata(pdev, core);
 
